data: {"item_id":"rs_891520","output_index":0,"sequence_number":289,"summary_index":0,"text":"We need to implement task 001 correctly. The previous attempt failed due to malformed tool call JSON (the exec command with embedded newlines and quotes causing JSON parsing errors). We need to create files using proper commands.\n\nWe have a repository at /home/agent/work. We need to implement server.js, maybe index.html and client-side code, and set up SQLite DB. No external dependencies allowed, but we can use node:sqlite module (experimental?). Node 22 includes node:sqlite (since v22). We'll use sqlite3 via node:sqlite. We'll create DB file at process.env.DB_PATH or default.\n\nDefine server routes: GET /health returns JSON. API endpoints: GET /api/projects returns list, POST /api/projects creates, GET /api/projects/:id returns one. Also static serve of public folder.\n\nImplement front-end as described.\n\nWe need to ensure project rows have data-testid=\"project-row\". The button Open project. On opening project page, show heading name and a Projects button linking back.\n\nPersist data using SQLite: table projects (id INTEGER PRIMARY KEY AUTOINCREMENT, name TEXT NOT NULL). Use prepared statements.\n\nMake sure to bind to 0.0.0.0 and port from env PORT default 8080. DB_PATH env default path maybe ./workboard.db.\n\nImplement npm start script in package.json.\n\nWe need to commit changes and output commit hash.\n\nLet's inspect repo.","type":"response.reasoning_summary_text.done"}

